WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.752
Guan Yu had died in battle, and the sixty-one-year-old Liu Bei, filled with grief and rage, personally led his army east.

00:00:07.952 --> 00:00:13.112
The Shu army marched east in a mighty host, advancing on Eastern Wu.

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:17.768
The Shu army pitched camps stretching for hundreds of li along the riverbank.

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:23.656
Wu's commander Lu Xun was young and composed; he held his defenses and would not come out to fight.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:29.008
Unable to break through after long attacks, the Shu army's spirit gradually sank.

00:00:29.208 --> 00:00:32.784
One night, deep in the darkness, Lu Xun ordered a fire attack on the Shu camps.

00:00:32.784 --> 00:00:37.896
Great flames blazed up, and the linked camps sank into a sea of fire.

00:00:38.096 --> 00:00:42.464
Liu Bei was badly defeated and fled in haste with his remaining troops.

00:00:42.464 --> 00:00:46.712
He withdrew to Baidicheng, his heart full of regret.

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:52.448
The Battle of Yiling gravely weakened Shu Han, and it never again had the strength for an eastern campaign.

